dia - Dedicated Internet Access (DIA) service for Cisco NSO 6.4

Configures a customer-facing PE interface (port or dot1Q sub-interface)
with a description and IPv4 address, and adds it as a passive interface
to the existing 'router isis 1' process. Supported NED: cisco-ios-cli.

'router isis 1' must already exist on the PE; the service only owns the
passive-interface entry. The service also refuses a port that already has
an IPv4 address, or a sub-interface that already exists.

Build and load:

  make all                                   # from repo root
  ncs_cli -C -u admin  ->  packages reload

Sample instance (port-mode):

  services dia CUSTOMER-A DIA-0001
   provider-edge device ios-0
    interface Ethernet0/3
     description  to_client3
     ipv4-address 100.64.16.1/29
     port-mode    true
  commit dry-run outformat native

  interface Ethernet0/3
   description "to_client3"
   ip address 100.64.16.1 255.255.255.248
  exit
  router isis 1
   passive-interface Ethernet0/3
  !

Sub-interface: set 'port-mode false' and 'vlan-id <1-4094>'; the service
creates Ethernet0/3.<vlan-id> with 'encapsulation dot1Q <vlan-id>'.
If 'description' is omitted it defaults to NSO:<customer-name>:<service-id>.
